# Security Baseline

- Never hardcode secrets, keys, tokens, or credentials.
- Validate and sanitize all external inputs.
- Encrypt data in transit and at rest in target designs.
- Mask PII/PHI in logs, traces, audits, and test artifacts.
- AuthN/Z coverage for protected APIs; audit logging for sensitive actions.
- Follow OWASP Top 10; dependency and SAST evidence before merge.
- Dedicated evidence packs: `/sast-scan`, `/dast-scan` (operator-owned localhost/staging only), `/threat-profile`. Never write exploits, PoCs, or attack payloads.
